{"id": "Dens1wBx1d9", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does KUMBHAKARNA sleep for six months? 😴 The gods were so terrified of his wish, a goddess hijacked his tongue.\n\nRavana's brother ate thousands of creatures as a newborn. In Indra's garden he ate seven apsaras and ten of Indra's followers, and when Indra struck him with the vajra, he ripped a tusk off Airavat and stabbed Indra with it.\n\nThen he did tapas for 10,000 years: in fire all summer, in water all winter. When Brahma came to grant his wish, the gods begged: \"Not him. Give him delusion instead.\" So Brahma sent Saraswati, goddess of speech, into his mouth, and Kumbhakarna said: \"I wish to SLEEP for many years!\" \"So be it.\" The moment she left, he froze: \"What came out of my mouth?!\" Brahma later eased it: six months asleep, one day awake.\n\nTo wake him for the war, they piled a mountain of meat, blew conches so loud that birds fell from the sky, and ran a thousand elephants over him. He woke up yawning, and hungry. 🙏\n\n(Valmiki Ramayana, Uttara Kanda 10; Yuddha Kanda 60–61)\n\nWho's the Kumbhakarna in YOUR house? Tag them all 👇 Save this and send it to the deepest sleeper you know.\n\nMore stories of Shiva and the gods: follow @therishikatha · rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n#kumbhakarna #ramayana #ravana #saraswati #brahma #valmikiramayana #hindumythology #sanatandharma #mythologystories #indianmythology #jaishriram #ramayanstories #mythology #sleep #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792293775, "like_count": 11107, "comment_count": 79, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1935252424117947a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 64.537, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNy1DXKbZQmGc4H850uRhUBAomH-TuPF0iJoRm97HxnS5LV-tvl